{
  "id": "p16",
  "title": "The Repair Shop on the Square",
  "titleZh": "广场边的修理铺",
  "topic": "手艺与街区",
  "paragraphs": [
    [
      {
        "en": "My father is ninety, and he still keeps a repair shop.",
        "zh": "我父亲九十岁了，还守着一间修理铺。"
      },
      {
        "en": "His office sits in the town centre, beside the square.",
        "zh": "他的办公室在镇中心，就在广场旁边。"
      },
      {
        "en": "He has worked at that bench a very long time.",
        "zh": "他在那张工作台前干了很久很久。"
      },
      {
        "en": "My dad builds clocks, creates lamps, and fixes every wheel.",
        "zh": "我爸修钟、做台灯，什么轮子都能修。"
      },
      {
        "en": "He really likes old brass parts more than cheap plastic ones.",
        "zh": "比起廉价的塑料件，他真的很喜欢旧黄铜零件。"
      },
      {
        "en": "People notice he is never silent while he works.",
        "zh": "人们发现他干活时从不沉默。"
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "en": "A mad little box arrives with a hole in its side.",
        "zh": "一只古怪的小盒子被送来，侧面破了个洞。"
      },
      {
        "en": "He found it travelling in a field west of the old house.",
        "zh": "那是他旅行时在老房子西边的一块地里捡到的。"
      },
      {
        "en": "The old man knocks it twice, and a warm blow escapes.",
        "zh": "老人敲了两下，一股热气冒了出来。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Something white hides inside, a small human figure.",
        "zh": "里面藏着个白色的东西，是个小小的人形。"
      },
      {
        "en": "His printed numbers show the degree of an interesting discovery.",
        "zh": "上面印着的数字显示出一个有趣发现的程度。"
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "en": "An arm turns the wheel in a steady direction and starts three lines.",
        "zh": "一条手臂带着轮子朝稳定方向转，起手画三条线。"
      },
      {
        "en": "He will build a second machine and introduce it to school.",
        "zh": "他要再做一台机器，把它介绍给学校。"
      },
      {
        "en": "The boy laughs and says the wooden wicket will work.",
        "zh": "男孩笑了，说那根木球门柱还能用。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Everyone stops to watch the metal arm move.",
        "zh": "所有人都停下来看那条金属手臂动。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Then he explains each step and praises the boy's clever hands.",
        "zh": "接着他讲解每一步，还夸男孩的手很巧。"
      },
      {
        "en": "\"You have a true gift,\" he says, \"and a very steady hand.\"",
        "zh": "“你有真天赋，”他说，“还有一双非常稳的手。”"
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "en": "Later, the shop smells of fried fish and evening tea.",
        "zh": "后来，铺子里飘着炸鱼和晚茶的味道。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A young woman brings an old dress back to a new life.",
        "zh": "一位年轻女子把一条旧裙子带回新的生活。"
      },
      {
        "en": "The cost does not bother her, and the bill is small.",
        "zh": "费用并不让她为难，账单也很小。"
      },
      {
        "en": "He often says a good repair is possible, so do not worry.",
        "zh": "他常说好好修一修总有办法，所以别担心。"
      },
      {
        "en": "He says the hole is no danger and the stain will go.",
        "zh": "他说那个洞不危险，污渍也会去掉。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Some children play football outside, and a flag waves nearby.",
        "zh": "外面有几个孩子在踢足球，旁边一面旗子在飘。"
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "en": "Then the shop closes at nine, except on cold winter match nights.",
        "zh": "然后铺子九点关门，只有寒冷的冬夜比赛除外。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Hard years can kill even a small shop, and danger is always near.",
        "zh": "艰难的年份能杀死一间小店，危险总在不远处。"
      },
      {
        "en": "My mother did not want me to marry a quiet man from the west.",
        "zh": "我母亲不想让我嫁给一个从西边来的安静男人。"
      },
      {
        "en": "That is how a small shop can happen, and how it grows.",
        "zh": "一间小店就是这样发生的，也是这样长大的。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A tiny bathroom sits behind the office, full of spare boxes.",
        "zh": "办公室后面有个小浴室，塞满了备用箱子。"
      }
    ]
  ],
